      "html": "<p>YazNot is a calm notebook built for one thing: not losing the sentence in your head. It runs offline on Windows, installs from the browser on your phone, and shows the same notes everywhere you sign in with the same account.</p>\n<p>This guide is intentionally short. Open the section you need, finish the task, and get back to writing. You can reopen it any time from the <strong>?</strong> button in the bottom-right corner or <strong>⋯ → User guide</strong>. The in-app guide works offline.</p>\n<h3>Three ideas</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>Device first, cloud second.</strong> A note is saved on this device before it syncs. Write without a connection; changes catch up when you are back online.</li><li><strong>Speech stays here.</strong> Speech-to-text runs entirely on your device. Audio is never sent to a server.</li><li><strong>Keep it calm.</strong> Sections, notes and a few good tools. Everything distracting stays behind a menu.</li></ul>"
